{
  "upload_type": "software",
  "title": "SynthPopCan",
  "description": "<p>SynthPopCan is research software for Canadian synthetic population work, including Statistics Canada margin/control table workflows, iterative proportional fitting, census microdata adapters, linked household/person model generation, explicit Census geography contracts, small-area calibration, national DA/ADA orchestration, governed enrichment sidecars, validation, and a local browser workbench.</p><p>Prepared model packages are distributed as separate archived records. Each is trained from a Statistics Canada Census Public Use Microdata File and carries the Statistics Canada Open Licence attribution notice, disclosure-review status, and file checksums. Generated populations are synthetic artifacts: they are not real Census records and must not be presented as confidential Statistics Canada information.</p><p>This software is independent research software. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by Statistics Canada or the Government of Canada.</p>",
